  "Partitions": {
    "setelement/3": "Tuple and integer index1..arity; copy tuple references and replace exactly one field; invalid combinations badarg. The result is a fresh nonempty tuple, without input mutation.",
    "append_element/2": "Tuple arity below16777215; copy references in order and append exact value reference. At/above the limit or a nontuple: badarg.",
    "insert_element/3": "Tuple and integer index1..arity+1; preserve prefix/suffix references and insert exact value. Invalid type/range badarg. Preserve pinned insert behavior; do not invent append-style extra arity validation.",
    "delete_element/2": "Tuple and integer index1..arity; preserve surviving references/order; single-element tuple produces canonical empty storage; invalid combinations badarg.",
    "make_tuple/2": "Integer size0..16777215; repeat the actual default reference; zero returns canonical empty storage; every other size badarg.",
    "make_tuple/3": "Same size/default construction, followed by proper list of two-tuples with indices1..size. Apply left-to-right, last duplicate wins; reject malformed entries/tails/indices. Allocation-before-initializer-validation follows pinned source.",
    "list_to_tuple/1": "Finite proper list of at most16777215 cells; preserve each element reference and order; nil produces canonical empty storage. Improper/nonslist/oversize inputs badarg. Early size refusal and complete native length scan have the same pure error outcome/arguments."
